<title>USA: US FTC moves to block MEDIQ merger.</title>
<headline>US FTC moves to block MEDIQ merger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission said Tuesday that it will ask a judge to block the $100 million merger of the nation's largest companies renting medical equipment, MEDIQ Inc. and Universal Hospital Services Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;The result will be higher rental prices because hospitals and hospital chains will not switch from renting to buying expensive equipment that may sit idle for long periods, even in the face of a signicant rental price increase,&quot; the FTC said.</p>
<p>The FTC voted 5-0 against the merger, which the FTC will challenge in a federal District Court.</p>
</text>
